  "exact_results": [
    "For q=(r,s,u) in complex three-space, literal Z=(r^2+s^2-u^2)/(2s), W=r^2-Z^2, and the vector map ordered (Z,W) are complex analytic wherever s is nonzero. The vector map is zero at (0,sigma,sigma).",
    "For real sigma>0 and 0<=delta<=sigma/4, all three closed-polydisc bounds ||r||,||s-sigma||,||u-sigma||<=delta imply s!=0, ||Z||<=4delta and ||W||<=17delta^2. A strict-polydisc corollary and the explicit nonzero actual denominator 2s are supplied. The extra paper restriction delta<=1 is unnecessary.",
    "For h>0 and delta<=h/16, the strict polydisc maps into ||Z||<=h/4, ||W||<h^2/2, ||s-sigma||<h/16. Neighborhood analyticity is explicitly restricted to the literal polydisc.",
    "For arbitrary complex q with s!=0, 2sZ=r^2+s^2-u^2 and W+(Z-s)^2=u^2. W+Z^2=r^2 holds unconditionally. These are complex polynomial squares, not Hermitian norm squares."
